# Mobile layout rules (joinUp)

- **Cards that sit side by side (horizontal ScrollView/FlatList) must have a height independent of
  their content.** Any text with `numberOfLines={N}` must reserve `minHeight = N * lineHeight`;
  otherwise a long title makes one card taller than its neighbours. `GameCard` reserves its title
  lines (`titleLines`; carousels pass 1 and ellipsize) — keep that if you touch it, and do the same for any new card component.
- **Never use `flex-1` / `flex: 1` on a child of an auto-height container** (card bodies, `children`
  slots, `overflow-hidden` cards). In React Native `flex: 1` means `flexBasis: 0`, so the child can be
  measured too short (depends on text wrapping, so it is intermittent) and its content is clipped by
  `overflow-hidden` — this was the "Join button cut off" bug on the home date list. Use `w-full` /
  natural height. `flex-1` is fine inside a `flex-row` for horizontal sharing.
- When adding a new card variant, check it on a device with: a 1-line title, a very long title (3+
  lines of text), and a long location string.
